deckle-kfxgen

This crate is a Rust port of kfxgen (https://github.com/jloutsch/kfxgen) at commit
ad38ec8f192126f8cf2b9b61814c6dabe3d12c52. The dump hook in tools/ref/kfxgen_hook runs inside
kfxgen and is covered by this notice too.

    kfxgen
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Justin Loutsch
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.

kfxgen is offered under version 3 of the licence only, not "or any later version". So this
crate and the hook are GPL-3.0-only, while the rest of Deckle is GPL-3.0-or-later. A program
built with this crate can be distributed under version 3. The licence text is the LICENSE file
at the root of the repository.

kfxgen includes a modified subset of kfxlib, from the KFX Input/Output plugins for calibre:

    Copyright (C) 2016-2025 John Howell <jhowell@acm.org>
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

Parts of this crate follow kfxlib's behaviour as kfxgen uses it: how a decimal is written, the
approximate locations and pages, and the count of `YJ_symbols` entries. The symbol names in
src/generate/standard_symbols.rs are kfxgen's own (kfxgen's NOTICE), not kfxlib's.

src/epub ports rules from calibre 9.18.0 (https://github.com/kovidgoyal/calibre, tag v9.18.0),
how it reads an EPUB into the book view kfxgen is given:

    calibre
    Copyright (C) 2006-2026 Kovid Goyal and the calibre contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

Files the port follows: src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plugins/epub_input.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plumber.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/reader.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/polish/upgrade.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/flatcss.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/guide.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/metadata.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/trimmanifest.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/__init__.py, src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/opf2.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/opf3.py, src/calibre/ebooks/metadata/book/base.py,
src/calibre/utils/date.py,
src/calibre/utils/localization.py and src/calibre/utils/xml_parse.py. The table of two-letter
language codes in src/epub/package.rs is calibre's (`iso639['2to3']` in
resources/localization/iso639.calibre_msgpack, built from the iso-codes package). The
iso-codes data is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1, as calibre's
COPYRIGHT file records for it (`Files: setup/iso*`).

src/dom ports calibre 9.18.0's reading of a book's XHTML into a tree, under the same notice:
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/parse_utils.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/chardet.py, src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/preprocess.py,
src/calibre/__init__.py, src/calibre/ebooks/html_entities.c and src/calibre/utils/speedup.c.

src/dom/structure.rs ports calibre 9.18.0's chapter marks and generated contents, under the
same notice: src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/structure.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/reader.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py and src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plumber.py.

src/css ports calibre 9.18.0's reading of a book's stylesheets into rules and its first
cascade, under the same notice: src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/stylizer.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/normalize_css.py, src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/preprocess.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/flatcss.py and src/calibre/customize/profiles.py. It also
ports src/tinycss/media3.py and src/tinycss/fonts3.py, which Kovid Goyal wrote for calibre's
copy of tinycss and which carry calibre's GPL v3 header, and follows how the tinycss parser
they build on (src/tinycss/css21.py and src/tinycss/tokenizer.py) reads a media query and a
font shorthand; no tinycss code is copied. calibre's COPYRIGHT file lists src/tinycss/* as:

    tinycss
    Copyright: Simon Sapin
    License: BSD

src/css/flatten.rs and src/css/fake_margins.rs port calibre 9.18.0's CSS flattener and its
removal of fake margins, under the same notice: src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/flatcss.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/page_margin.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/stylizer.py
(`Style.lineHeight`, `Style.fontSize`), src/calibre/ebooks/__init__.py (`unit_convert`) and
src/calibre/customize/profiles.py (`fnums`). Class names are made ASCII with the deunicode crate
(BSD-3-Clause) where calibre uses its own transliteration.

src/css/style.rs ports calibre 9.18.0's style values, under the same notice:
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/stylizer.py (`Style`, `validate_color`), src/calibre/ebooks/__init__.py
(`unit_convert`, `UNIT_RE`) and src/calibre/customize/profiles.py (`fsizes`, the screen size).
The colour pattern is css_parser's CSS 2.1 `color`, read from calibre.

src/book.rs runs those ports in calibre 9.18.0's order and reads each file's stylesheets as its
Stylizer finds them, under the same notice: src/calibre/ebooks/conversion/plumber.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/stylizer.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/base.py,
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/reader.py, src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/structure.py and
src/calibre/ebooks/oeb/transforms/flatcss.py.

The tables in src/css/defaults.rs are calibre's (`DEFAULTS`, `INHERITED`). src/css also
follows the behaviour of css_parser 1.1.1, the CSS library calibre runs (a fork of cssutils,
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3 or later); no css_parser code is
copied, its behaviour was read from calibre.

